WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.550 --> 00:00:06.960
There's a wonderful systematic
review of a large number

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.980
of studies that have looked

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.360
at mental training and visualization.

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.420
What's effective, what's
less effective across a bunch

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:14.790
of different disciplines that
include education, medicine,

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.680
music, psychology, and sports.

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:17.970
We will provide a link to this paper

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.680
in the show note captions,
but the title of the paper

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.540
is "Best practice for motor imagery:

00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:23.130
a systematic literature review

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.840
on motor imagery training elements

00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:26.400
in five different disciplines."

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:27.450
As the title suggests,

00:00:27.450 --> 00:00:30.780
it's mainly for motor imagery training,

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:32.880
but it extends into music,

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:36.120
which of course involves
motor training and execution,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.160
but as well as education.

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:39.120
This review establishes

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.380
a number of different important things.

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:41.430
I'm going to read off

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:44.820
some of the key or highlight takeaways.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.190
For instance, I described principle one

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.870
of effective mental training

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.020
and visualization, which is
that the visualization be brief

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.880
and it be simple and it be repeated.

00:00:53.880 --> 00:00:58.350
May ask how many times that
very brief, 5 to 15 second

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.610
exercise of going through some
routine should be repeated.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:05.070
Well, different studies
have used different ranges

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:08.550
of, let's call them repetitions
in a given training session,

00:01:08.550 --> 00:01:11.400
but the number that seems
to be most effective

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:16.350
is somewhere between 50
and 75 repeats per session.

00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.440
That brings about the question
of how long one should rest

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.420
between each repeat.

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:22.350
This gets a little tricky

00:01:22.350 --> 00:01:24.600
depending on what you're trying to do.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.700
Remember that we have
this kind of threshold

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:28.680
of about 15 seconds for completion

00:01:28.680 --> 00:01:30.090
of the entire motor sequence.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.320
Let's say what you're trying to do,

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.720
like a golf swing takes you 5 seconds

00:01:33.720 --> 00:01:35.170
to imagine in your mind's eye

00:01:36.180 --> 00:01:37.380
from the point where you,

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:38.880
let's just say have the ball on the tee.

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:40.860
You bring the the golf club up,

00:01:40.860 --> 00:01:43.470
you might reposition your
feet just a little bit,

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.990
you know, that kind of a little
wiggle that golf golfers do,

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:46.890
and then the swing.

00:01:46.890 --> 00:01:49.920
If that whole thing takes five
seconds in your mind's eye

00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:52.230
and roughly five seconds
in the real world,

00:01:52.230 --> 00:01:53.880
well then you'd be able
to repeat it, of course,

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.650
3 times in 15 seconds.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.620
That would be one repetition,

00:01:58.620 --> 00:02:00.060
even though you're doing it 3 times.

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:02.220
So it's one 15 second epoch

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:05.040
as it's sometimes called, E-P-O-C-H epoch,

00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:06.480
and then you would rest

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.810
for an approximately
equivalent amount of time,

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.840
15 seconds or so, and then repeat.

00:02:12.840 --> 00:02:15.000
And rest 15 seconds or so,

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.480
and then repeat, rest 15
seconds and then repeat.

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:21.030
Again, 3 golf swings
within that 15 seconds.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:21.960
Rest, 15 seconds.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:25.140
3 golf swings within that
15 seconds. Rest 15 seconds.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.450
Truth told, these epochs

00:02:27.450 --> 00:02:30.780
and these rest periods
do not need to be exact.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:32.400
You could imagine, for instance,

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.860
that you get 3 repetitions

00:02:34.860 --> 00:02:37.140
of the swing within 14 seconds.

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:38.310
Well then do you do another one

00:02:38.310 --> 00:02:40.110
or do you wait until the
end of that 15 seconds?

00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.480
I encourage you not to obsess too much

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.950
about those sorts of points.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:46.050
Rather you want to do as many repeats

00:02:46.050 --> 00:02:50.430
as you can in about a 15 second epoch

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:52.680
and then rest for about 15 seconds,

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:56.610
and then repeat for a total
of 50 to 75 repetitions,

00:02:56.610 --> 00:02:58.650
which might not sound like a lot

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.483
to some of you,

00:02:59.483 --> 00:03:02.520
might sound like an awful
lot to others of you.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:05.010
To me, it sounds like a lot,
you know, 50 repetitions

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.090
of something and where you're trying

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:08.730
to concentrate in your mind's
eye on getting something

00:03:08.730 --> 00:03:10.860
accomplished over and over, over again

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:13.020
in exactly the same way
might seem like a lot.

00:03:13.020 --> 00:03:16.620
We know based on the learning
literature that your ability

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.710
to successfully perform
something in the real world

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.690
will lend itself to better performance

00:03:21.690 --> 00:03:24.210
of that thing in the imagined world,

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.530
within your mind's eye.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:27.510
That's also one of these sort of does.

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:30.270
But if you're trying to
get better at something

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:31.860
that you've never performed before,

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:33.060
you really should know that.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:33.893
The mental training

00:03:33.893 --> 00:03:37.260
and visualization is
probably not the best augment

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:38.640
to that real world training

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:41.370
until you're able to
perform it successfully

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:44.490
in the real world, at
least some of the time.

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:47.610
Mental training and
visualization can be effective,

00:03:47.610 --> 00:03:50.700
however, at increasing the accuracy

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.530
or the frequency at which you can do

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.840
that real world behavior.

00:03:54.840 --> 00:03:57.060
So if normally you're only
getting the correct swing

00:03:57.060 --> 00:04:00.150
or you're only hitting
the golf ball correctly,

00:04:00.150 --> 00:04:01.230
say 10% of the time,

00:04:01.230 --> 00:04:02.340
mental training and visualization

00:04:02.340 --> 00:04:04.470
can really help bring that number up.

00:04:04.470 --> 00:04:05.940
But it is important that you are able

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:08.760
to successfully complete that
motor task in the real world.

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.310
Similarly for performance
of cognitive tasks.

00:04:11.310 --> 00:04:15.510
So say for instance,
speaking a new language,

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:16.830
you might ask, well, gosh,

00:04:16.830 --> 00:04:18.570
what in the landscape of speaking

00:04:18.570 --> 00:04:21.720
a new language can be
restricted to 5 to 15 seconds

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:23.790
where I could repeat it
anywhere from, you know,

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:26.760
1 to 3 times in a given
epoch and then rest

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:29.280
and then keep repeating 50 to 75 times?

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:31.560
Well, there, I would encourage
you to pick something

00:04:31.560 --> 00:04:34.200
that you are able to
do perhaps very slowly.

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:36.960
So to speak a particular sentence,

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.660
but with some challenge
in getting the accent

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:40.860
and the enunciation right.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:43.470
But you've completed
it successfully before

00:04:43.470 --> 00:04:46.080
and you want to get more
smooth or more fluid with it.

00:04:46.080 --> 00:04:47.940
Likewise, for, you know, playing piano

00:04:47.940 --> 00:04:49.980
or guitar, again, you have to translate

00:04:49.980 --> 00:04:51.360
to the specific cognitive

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:55.860
and/or motor activity that
you are seeking to improve at.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:59.730
But those epochs lasting 5 to 15 seconds

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:02.250
are really the cornerstone of
an effective mental training

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:03.420
and visualization practice.

00:05:03.420 --> 00:05:05.340
And the repeated nature of it,

00:05:05.340 --> 00:05:08.190
50 to 75 repetitions in a given session

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:11.220
is also another cornerstone of
an effective mental training

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:12.960
and visualization practice.

00:05:12.960 --> 00:05:14.550
So says this review

00:05:14.550 --> 00:05:15.510
and some of the other papers

00:05:15.510 --> 00:05:17.820
that I'm going to get to in a few moments.

00:05:17.820 --> 00:05:19.831
Now, one of the other key components

00:05:19.831 --> 00:05:22.020
of a successful mental training

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.590
and visualization practice
is how often you perform

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:27.660
that mental training and
visualization practice.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:31.740
And again, a number of different
studies have looked at this

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:32.970
through a number of different lenses,

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:37.590
meaning anywhere from
2 to 8 times per week.

00:05:37.590 --> 00:05:40.680
It does appear that
performing these sessions

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:43.020
anywhere from 3 to 5 times per week

00:05:43.020 --> 00:05:44.670
is going to be effective.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:46.410
We could perhaps even say most effective

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:50.400
because most of the, let's just
call it the strongest data,

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:53.850
really point to repeating
these 50 to 75 trials

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:56.370
of the same thing 3 to 5 times per week.

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.190
So you can come up with a
number that's reasonable for you

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:01.980
to do consistently, and you might ask,

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:05.400
do you have to continue to
perform the mental training

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.200
and visualization forever?

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.320
And the good news is the
answer to that question is no.

00:06:10.320 --> 00:06:14.550
It does seem that once you
have what's called consolidated

00:06:14.550 --> 00:06:16.080
the motor performance

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.670
or the cognitive performance of something,

00:06:17.670 --> 00:06:19.620
it can be further supported

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:23.550
or reinforced, that is
consolidated in the neural circuits

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:25.110
that are responsible for performing

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.360
that mental or physical task.

00:06:27.360 --> 00:06:30.450
So in other words, once you
are performing that cognitive

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:33.300
or motor task in a way that's satisfactory

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:35.130
or perhaps just improved,

00:06:35.130 --> 00:06:36.420
perhaps you're not a hundred percent,

00:06:36.420 --> 00:06:38.160
but it's improved in the real world,

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:40.350
you don't need to continue
to do mental training

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.930
and visualization to maintain

00:06:42.930 --> 00:06:44.370
that real world performance.

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:45.203
So that's a good thing.

00:06:45.203 --> 00:06:47.340
In fact, the ideal situation

00:06:47.340 --> 00:06:50.640
would be then to pick a different sequence

00:06:50.640 --> 00:06:51.750
or thing that you're trying to learn

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:54.390
and do mental training and
visualization for that.

00:06:54.390 --> 00:06:56.550
I perhaps might've misspoke there,

00:06:56.550 --> 00:06:58.470
although I don't want to edit this out.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:02.490
I misspoke in the sense that,
again, I said for the thing

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:04.710
that you're trying to learn,
remember, mental training

00:07:04.710 --> 00:07:06.990
and visualization is
going to be most effective

00:07:06.990 --> 00:07:11.190
for building up the
number of accurate trials,

00:07:11.190 --> 00:07:13.470
or your ability to do something

00:07:13.470 --> 00:07:16.800
with a greater frequency of
something that you're already

00:07:16.800 --> 00:07:17.700
capable of doing

00:07:17.700 --> 00:07:21.210
or have done at least
once in the real world.

00:07:21.210 --> 00:07:22.620
This is not to say that mental training

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:26.490
and visualization can't be
used to acquire new skills.

00:07:26.490 --> 00:07:28.080
It can in principle,

00:07:28.080 --> 00:07:30.240
but it has been shown to be most effective

00:07:30.240 --> 00:07:31.500
for enhancing the speed

00:07:31.500 --> 00:07:33.180
and the accuracy of skills

00:07:33.180 --> 00:07:35.760
that one has already
demonstrated some degree

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:38.130
of proficiency at in the real world.

00:07:38.130 --> 00:07:39.990
I think that's important to point out

00:07:39.990 --> 00:07:42.660
because we often hear mental
training and visualization

00:07:42.660 --> 00:07:44.250
and this equivalence of perceptual

00:07:44.250 --> 00:07:46.590
and motor experiences in our
mind's eye to the real world,

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:47.423
and we think, oh,

00:07:47.423 --> 00:07:49.080
all we have to do is
imagine doing something

00:07:49.080 --> 00:07:50.970
and we will get better at it.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.650
And unfortunately, that's not the case.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:55.230
The good news is, however,
if you can do something once,

00:07:55.230 --> 00:07:57.270
even very slowly in the real world

00:07:57.270 --> 00:08:00.450
and then you bring it
to the mental imagery

00:08:00.450 --> 00:08:01.620
and visualization domain,

00:08:01.620 --> 00:08:03.030
you can get much faster at it in a way

00:08:03.030 --> 00:08:06.019
that really does translate
back to the real world.

00:08:06.019 --> 00:08:08.686
[MUSIC PLAYING]

